# Copy to `.env.local` to override for yourself (`.env.local` and `*.local` are gitignored).

# Where the API lives. The default '/api' is correct both in development (Vite proxies it
# to the backend, see vite.config.ts) and in production (the backend serves the built app
# on its own origin, so there is no CORS anywhere).
# VITE_API_BASE=/api

# Set to 'false' to disable the in-browser MSW mocks and talk to the real backend.
# `npm run dev:api` already does this via .env.api.
# VITE_USE_MOCKS=false

# Only needed if the backend is not on 127.0.0.1:8000. Vite reads this, not the app.
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
